stion) are actually your immune system fighting the virus, not just the virus itself doing damage. So even if you killed the virus early, you might already have triggered those symptoms. By the time you feel sick and reach for a cure, the virus has often already peaked, and all that’s left is your body’s cleanup operation. So when people say it’s difficult, it’s not that scientists haven’t tried—it’s that the cold is a moving target made of hundreds of viral shapes that change constantly, and society hasn’t made it a top priority. I hope that helps clarify things. If you’d like, I can explain why some other viral diseases (like smallpox) were easier to eradicate.
